2025-12-01T18:27:00Z - Git Progress Service Implementation
================================================================================
Author: Copilot CLI

Summary:
Implemented GitPython-based push/pull/clone operations with structured progress 
reporting, integrated with the Job Registry, and bridged to explorer WebSocket.

Files Created:
- app/libs/git_service.py (new, ~400 lines)
  - CallbackProgress(RemoteProgress) - GitPython progress wrapper
  - git_push_with_progress() - push with callback
  - git_pull_with_progress() - pull with callback  
  - git_clone_with_progress() - clone with callback
  - @register_job_handler("git_push")
  - @register_job_handler("git_pull")
  - @register_job_handler("git_clone")

Files Modified:
- app/apps/file_editor_cm6/explorer_ws.py
  - Added job listener bridge in ExplorerDispatcher
  - _pump_job_events() task forwards job:progress to WS clients
  - handle_git_push/pull now create jobs instead of direct calls
  - Added handle_git_clone for WS-based clone with progress

- app/apps/file_editor_cm6/static/js/explorer.js
  - Added job:progress event handler
  - Added git:pushStarted/pullStarted/cloneStarted handlers
  - Added showGitProgressBar()/hideGitProgressBar() helpers
  - Ephemeral progress bar at top of git footer
  - Right-aligned progress text in status row

Architecture:
1. Push/Pull/Clone buttons trigger job creation via WS
2. Job runs in background thread with GitPython
3. Progress callbacks update job state
4. Job manager broadcasts to listeners
5. ExplorerDispatcher filters and forwards to WS clients
6. Frontend renders ephemeral progress bar

Not Changed:
- Existing CLI-based git status/diff/log/stage/commit (still subprocess)
- Job Registry core (app/libs/jobs.py)
- Framework shells architecture
